# Robot personality — integrated behavior, not CLI jank

Cain shows these robots to people. They must **just work** from physical inputs on the bot — buttons, sensors, time of day — without opening a laptop or remembering shell commands.

## Do

- Add behavior as **part of the robot's firmware or always-on brain** (ROS node, service, docker compose default stack).
- Trigger from **on-bot inputs**: Go button, E-stop, ToF, IMU, wheel ticks, battery, schedule.
- Use **separate PlatformIO envs** only for bench/hardware bring-up (`motor_test`, `c3_bench`, `s3_min`) — that's fine.
- Brain logic lives on the **NUC brain** (`/data/swarm/robot-swarm-brain`) as services that start with the fleet — not one-off scripts Cain must run.

## Don't

- Don't ship features as **standalone scripts** that require `ssh`, `docker compose --profile`, or memorized bash to demo.
- Don't add "run this first, then that" runbooks for normal operation.
- Don't make Cain the sysadmin during a demo — the robot should wake up and do its thing.

## When adding a feature, ask

> Can someone press Go (or equivalent) and see this work without a terminal?

If no — redesign it into firmware, the default brain container, or an automatic trigger (sensor, timer, session state).
